@how_to_play
new-page: true

= How to play

You lead the **Ruusan Caucus**: a loose alliance of reform-minded senators from worlds like Alderaan, Chandrila, Corellia and Rodia. History says that over the next fourteen years the Republic will vote itself into an Empire, with thunderous applause. Your task is to stop that from happening, and to leave the Republic stronger than you found it.

**Turns.** Each turn you play **one card** from your hand. Draw cards from the *Caucus Affairs* deck (your own bloc's work) and, once you hold a seat in the governing coalition or a committee chair, from the *Senate Affairs* deck. Your **advisors** are pinned cards. Each can act once every few turns without using up your turn. Most turns cover a quarter of a year. During crises they shrink to months, and in the final hours to days.

**Events.** Between turns, the galaxy moves. Events fire on historical dates and in response to the state of the Republic. Many of them let you choose how the Caucus responds.

**What matters.** Keep an eye on the left-hand panel:

• *Political capital* is your currency. You earn it each year from patrons, and it is spent on most important actions.

• *Faith in the Republic*, *corruption* and *fear* shape the whole Senate. Palpatine feeds on corruption and fear.

• *Emergency powers* measure how far the Senate has surrendered its authority to the Chancellor.

• *Evidence* measures what you can prove about the Sith. Accusing anyone without proof will destroy you.

• *Senate resolve* measures how seriously the Senate takes the threat to its own power. Many strong countermeasures need it.

• *Separatism* in the Rim and the corporate worlds decides whether the Republic goes to war.

**Many roads.** You can deny Palpatine the Chancellery, clean up the Senate, heal the Outer Rim, hunt for the Sith, bind the emergency powers with sunset clauses, win the peace, prepare loyal forces, or save a troubled young Jedi. No single road is enough. All of them carry risks.

The **Holocron** link at the top of the page explains the factions, blocs and systems in more detail.

**Play it like an app.** Opened from the web in Edge or Chrome, the **Install game** link at the top adds Thunderous Applause to your Start menu and desktop. It then opens in its own window with one click and works offline.

*This is an unofficial, non-commercial fan work. It borrows from both canon and Legends, and wanders off into alternate history from the very first turn.*

